{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1409921-hedge-witchery","id":1409921,"title":"Hedge-witchery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-23T09:19:37-07:00","id":1409921,"title":"Hedge-witchery","content":"My young witch player is wanting to make charms and herbal remedies; she's not Awakened. Are there any extant systems for CoD that deal with such things, or should I just wing it? She has Holistic Awareness, but I was looking for something more specific.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T10:23:34-07:00","id":1409929,"title":"","content":"Really minor supernatural things would probably use the Build Equipment rules (<b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>, p. 100), likely off Occult (charms) or Medicine/Survival (herbal remedies). For bigger things, Supernatural Merits might be in order (assuming the character is mortal). <b>Hurt Locker</b> has some good options (Bless Amulet, Curse Effigy, and Evil Eye) for hedge magic, while the corebook ones mostly have a &quot;psychic powers&quot; flair.<br /> <br /> Simple Specialties can also help with the feel of the character, particularly enhanced with Merits like Area of Expertise or Interdisciplinary Specialty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T10:24:18-07:00","id":1409930,"title":"","content":"Mystical equipment is a thing players can make, and wards against supernatural beings are likewise able. There is a merit in Hurt Locker (Bless Amulet) specifically for making charms that prevent people from being possessed, too. Otherwise, the charms/amulets your character makes are about as effective as you let them. Herbal remedies _are_ a thing in real life though. For that they can probably craft them like any other crafting attempt but with Medicine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T10:45:49-07:00","id":1409935,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with using the Build Equipment rules. <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/208162/Dark-Eras-To-the-Strongest-Mage-the-Awakening?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">To the Strongest</a> in the original <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/178583/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Dark-Eras?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Dark Eras</a> also offers some suggestions for un-Awakened witches. <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/282275/Night-Horrors-Shunned-by-the-Moon?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Shunned by the Moon</a> features Shadow Occultists, who bargain with spirits for magical powers. Mortals can also use Tokens from Changeling as long as they fulfill the loophole, so that could give you a mechanical framework for making charms, whether or not they actually come from the Hedge. The Guidelines for creating your own are in the chapter I wrote for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/306076/Oak-Ash-and-Thorn-The-Changeling-The-Lost-Second-Edition-Companion?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Oak, Ash, and Thorn</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T13:22:44-07:00","id":1409958,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the suggestions, I will delve into them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T19:02:42-07:00","id":1409995,"title":"","content":"Hurt locker also has a small bit about making charms without needing supernatural merits (HL 62). <br /> <br /> There is also HtV witchfinder but it would take some adjustments to bring up to 2e (I've worked one out I feel good about), the ritual magic in particular that allows one to preform magic with multiple participants is rather thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T19:51:25-07:00","id":1410001,"title":"","content":"On the Storyteller's Vault there is also the book <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/260310/Second-Sight-Third-Eye?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45760_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">Second Sight: Third Eye</a> which deals with mortal psychic powers and hedge mages and perhaps <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/309674/A-Deal-With-Darkness?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=0_0_45760_0_0_0_0\" target=\"_blank\">A Deal with Darkness</a> which is about forming supernatural pacts. While not 'official' they are <i>very </i>well written and I don't hesitate to include them in chronicles games I run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-23T22:46:15-07:00","id":1410016,"title":"","content":"She could try to harness the spirit power of a herbal medicine shop, a hospital or a sacred healing site. More details can be found here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231346-those-who-call-to-spirits-human-occultists\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231346-those-who-call-to-spirits-human-occultists\"> Those Who Call To Spirits - Human Occultists - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231346-those-who-call-to-spirits-human-occultists\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1231346-those-who-call-to-spirits-human-occultists </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> How about a new kind of human antagonist, eh? Few humans have the perceptiveness to discover the world of spirits; of those, fewer still have the mental resilience to deal with such a discovery, and yet fewer have the wits and cleverness to actually survive interactions with the alien beings slithering through the fabric of reality. There&rsquo;s no handy user manual for the budding shaman or would-be witch, no-one who can help and explain what&rsquo;s going on when you&rsquo;ve caught the attention of things with too many eyes that are made from raw emotion. Libraries on the Shadow and its denizens are </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T04:45:56-07:00","id":1410039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1409921-hedge-witchery?p=1409929#post1409929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really minor supernatural things would probably use the Build Equipment rules (<b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>, p. 100), likely off Occult (charms) or Medicine/Survival (herbal remedies). For bigger things, Supernatural Merits might be in order (assuming the character is mortal). <b>Hurt Locker</b> has some good options (Bless Amulet, Curse Effigy, and Evil Eye) for hedge magic, while the corebook ones mostly have a &quot;psychic powers&quot; flair.<br /> <br /> Simple Specialties can also help with the feel of the character, particularly enhanced with Merits like Area of Expertise or Interdisciplinary Specialty.</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes a bit more development, but don't underestimate the mileage you can get with Occult &quot;Equipment&quot; here - it doesn't even need to be represented as physical charms and the like. Just as Plans are an abstract type of Equipment, Occult Equipment could be a prepared spell or invoked blessing, and serve as the justification for allowing the bearer to perform an Attribute + Skill roll to achieve an effect. You can't do surgery without tools no matter how good your Medicine, and you can't set fire on people with your gaze without the Eyes of Flame blessing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T17:27:07-07:00","id":1410166,"title":"","content":"Excellent ideas. I admit I never looked at building equipment before. That can work splendidly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T19:10:51-07:00","id":1410183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1409921-hedge-witchery?p=1409995#post1409995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hurt locker also has a small bit about making charms without needing supernatural merits (HL 62).<br /> <br /> There is also HtV witchfinder but it would take some adjustments to bring up to 2e (I've worked one out I feel good about), the ritual magic in particular that allows one to preform magic with multiple participants is rather thematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's useful, because in the witch's culture ordinary people say charms and make amulets and protective devices as a matter of course. The witches just pack more of a punch when they do it.<br /> <br /> I'd like to see your updated ritual system.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2203-corrigan","name":"Corrigan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}